---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="My Story | Built By Raza"
  description="The story behind Built By Raza — a career in networking, telecommunications, solution architecture, learning and building."
>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">MY STORY</p>

      <h1>
        From building networks to designing solutions.
      </h1>

      <p class="intro">
        My journey through more than two decades of networking,
        telecommunications and technology — and why I still consider
        myself a student of the industry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">2004 · THE BEGINNING</p>
        <h2>It started with networking.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          I began my career in networking in 2004. What started as a
          profession quickly became something I genuinely enjoyed:
          understanding how systems communicate, how networks are built,
          and how technology can be used to solve real problems.
        </p>

        <p>
          Those early years gave me the technical foundation that would
          shape the rest of my career.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">2009 · DUBAI</p>
        <h2>Into the Internet backbone.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          In 2009, I joined a large Internet service provider in Dubai,
          working as an engineer in its Internet backbone department.
        </p>

        <p>
          This was where networking moved from theory and smaller
          environments into large-scale telecommunications infrastructure.
          Working around an ISP backbone gave me firsthand experience with
          the systems and engineering decisions that keep large networks
          connected.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">A MAJOR MILESTONE</p>
        <h2>Earning my CCIE.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          One of the milestones I'm most proud of is earning my Cisco
          Certified Internetwork Expert certification.
        </p>

        <p>
          For me, the CCIE represented more than passing an exam. It was
          the result of years of study, hands-on experience and a commitment
          to understanding networking at a much deeper level.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">SATELLITE NETWORKS</p>
        <h2>A project that stayed with me.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          Another particularly meaningful chapter of my career was working
          on satellite networking for Airbus in Abu Dhabi.
        </p>

        <p>
          It gave me the opportunity to apply my networking background in
          a very different environment and work on complex communications
          infrastructure where reliability, architecture and engineering
          all had to come together.
        </p>

        <p>
          It remains one of the projects I am most proud to have been
          involved with.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">2021 · A NEW PERSPECTIVE</p>
        <h2>From engineering networks to designing solutions.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          In 2021, my career began moving into pre-sales engineering and
          solution architecture.
        </p>

        <p>
          The focus became broader. Instead of looking only at the
          technology, I was increasingly starting with the customer:
          understanding the problem, identifying the requirements and
          designing the right solution.
        </p>

        <p>
          It brought together years of engineering experience with another
          side of technology that I enjoy — turning complex technical ideas
          into practical solutions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">TODAY · STILL LEARNING</p>
        <h2>The next chapter is already being built.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          Technology doesn't stand still, and neither should an architect.
        </p>

        <p>
          Today I'm building on my networking and solution architecture
          experience by going deeper into cloud, automation and AI
          infrastructure.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't see this as starting over. I see it as adding new layers
          to the foundation I've spent more than two decades building.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">BEYOND TECHNOLOGY</p>
        <h2>The builder mindset doesn't stop at work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          My curiosity isn't limited to networks and technology. I enjoy
          reef aquariums, gardening, DIY projects and figuring out how to
          fix or improve things around the house.
        </p>

        <p>
          The subject may be completely different, but I often find myself
          following the same process: understand how something works,
          identify the problem, experiment, learn and improve it.
        </p>

        <p>
          That's really what Built By Raza is about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
    </main>

    
  


<style>
  

  .container {
    width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 40px));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  

  

  .hero {
    padding: 120px 0 110px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 24px;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.7rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 95px 0;
  }

  .alt {
    background: #f7f7f8;
  }

  .story-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .copy p {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    

    .hero {
      padding: 80px 0;
    }

    .story-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
</BaseLayout>